;Match details

* '''Match 1: KAZUKI def. Tanaka.''' The block favourite's opening statement. Tanaka — the Cannon Club brawler — tried to drag the match into a fight: forearms, chops, brawling on the floor. KAZUKI refused to brawl. He used speed — springboard dropkicks, a tope con giro, the missile dropkick — and kept Tanaka off balance for 11 minutes. The finish: Tanaka went for the Bulldog lariat, KAZUKI ducked, hit the Pele kick, climbed, and delivered the Twin Star Press. 1-2-3 at 11:42. KAZUKI's fourth consecutive win since the Kuroshio reunion at [[NOPW Wednesday Episode 10|Episode 10]]. '''Crowd:''' MEGA POP for KAZUKI's entrance. '''KAZUKI''' chants. HEAT for Tanaka's brawling. POP for the tope con giro. BIG POP for the Twin Star Press. '''KAZUKI''' chants after.

* '''Match 2: Jusuf def. Ishida.''' The most uncomfortable match of the tournament so far. Ishida — the veteran who drew the blueprint against [[The Marauder]] at Episode 10 — tried the same approach: mat work, leg attacks, ring awareness. Jusuf did not engage with any of it. He did not bump for Ishida's strikes. He did not sell the leg work. He walked through Ishida's offense, caught a dragon screw attempt, and locked in the mosaraza kneebar in the center of the ring. Ishida held on as long as he could — 40 seconds — then tapped at 8:56. Jusuf released the hold, stood up, and walked out without acknowledging the crowd. The fastest win of the tournament so far. '''Crowd:''' HEAT for Jusuf's entrance. Uneasy silence during the match — the crowd did not know how to react. GASPS when Jusuf no-sold the strikes. '''TAP''' chants at Ishida before he submitted — the crowd begging him to save himself. HEAT as Jusuf walked out. '''THIS IS WRESTLING''' chants for Ishida as he left.

* '''Match 3: Taumafa def. Ono.''' The Strong Openweight Champion against the former World Television Champion. The size gap was the story: Taumafa, the Vaiahi giant, against Ono, the youngest entrant in the field at 24. Ono fought with everything — dropkicks to the knee, a tornado DDT, a missile dropkick that staggered the giant. Taumafa absorbed it all and answered with power: samoan drops, a running hip attack, corner splashes. The finish: Taumafa hoisted Ono up and delivered the giant powerbomb at 13:20. Ono kicked out at 2.8 — the crowd erupted — but Taumafa covered again for the clean three. After the match, Taumafa helped Ono up and nodded to him — the nod of an older cousin to a younger one. '''Crowd:''' POP for Taumafa's entrance. '''ONO''' chants for the young lion. Respectful POP for Ono. GASPS for the powerbomb. ERUPTION when Ono kicked out at 2.8. Respectful applause after — the crowd recognized a passing-of-the-guard moment that did not pass.

* '''Match 4: Takagi def. Kuroki.''' The match of the night. The Dragon vs. the Black Iron — two of the stiffest strikers in NOPW, both strong-style standouts, both fighting for early control of Block B. The match was 17 minutes of forearms, suplexes, and fighting spirit. Kuroki hit the Black Iron Bomb — Takagi kicked out at 2.9. Takagi hit the Dragon suplex — Kuroki kicked out at 2.85. The finish: Takagi ducked a lariat and hit the Dragon lariat — full speed — at 17:05. Clean pin. Both men received a standing ovation. '''Crowd:''' BUILD for both entrances. '''TAKAGI''' and '''KUROKI''' dueling chants. '''THIS IS WRESTLING''' during the strike exchanges. GASPS for the Black Iron Bomb kickout. GASPS for the Dragon suplex kickout. ERUPTION for the Dragon lariat. Standing ovation after.

* '''Match 5: Diallo def. Reyes.''' The Hammer vs. the Cobra. Reyes — the CHAOS technician and tag team specialist — used his speed and joint manipulation to keep Diallo off balance for 10 minutes. Diallo's Asikyran wrestling background showed in the exchanges — takedowns, gutwrenches, hammer strikes. The finish: Reyes went for the Cobra Twist — Diallo powered out, hoisted him up, and delivered the Hammer Slam at 12:31. Clean pin. '''Crowd:''' MIXED for Diallo. POP for Reyes's joint work. GASPS for the Hammer Slam. Respectful applause after.

